window.docContents[181].resolve({"/Judgments-and-domains/Static-judgments/#Core-C______--Judgments-and-domains--Static-judgments":{"contents":"The judgment  states that the expression  has type  in the context . One rule per constructor of Expr.Some of the implementations are partial, so Lean records opaque constants that carry the type and not the body, and no property of them is proved here.\n\nThe judgment  holds for the expressions that denote a location, a variable, *e, e.f, e->f and e[i].The implementations are partial, so Lean records opaque constants that carry the type and not the body, and no property of them is proved here.\n\nThe judgment  states that the command  is well typed and extends  to , so that a declaration reaches the following commands of the sequence. The return type  of the enclosing function is an implicit parameter.Some of the implementations are partial, so Lean records opaque constants that carry the type and not the body, and no property of them is proved here.\n\n","context":"Core C++\u0009Judgments and domains","header":"2.2. Static judgments","id":"/Judgments-and-domains/Static-judgments/#Core-C______--Judgments-and-domains--Static-judgments"}});